findings.claim:
New in C6e, a side effect of C6e-4's top exception (atTop = scrollY < 8).

At these short landscape windows the dots are already in the window at the top. The bar therefore:
- comes up on arrival;
- goes ('wait', the between-hold) after the first 8-10 px of scroll;
- slides back up every time the page returns within 8 px of the top.
A small drag or wheel turn near the top toggles it each time.

OLD waited at these windows: no bar until the inline ask, 37-60 px further down.

While up on arrival, the bar hides page text:
- 932x430: the product line (370-426 behind the bar at 365);
- 1100x450: 'Color: Acid' (389-412, bar at 385);
- 1280x480: 'Color: Acid' (398-421) sliced by the bar at 415.
This is the same family as C6d GB-4 (two slides within a short scroll).

