- y 493 and 497 land on div.ask-bar;
- y 499 and 501 fire the bar's mailto link on Tropos, Mantle and Core;
- the view never changes.
The same 15 px overlap appears after in-page arrivals: a family tile, a name in 'At the bar', and the home page's 'Meet Tropos' (/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-super-hot/f4a25b5c-7cd5-585d-b4f3-c7ba36b6c676/scratchpad/gate/c6e/skeptic-gallery-and-bar/out/navflow-a.txt).

One arithmetic slip: the thumbnails' centre is 477, not 469. It is still above 488, so the coordinator's centre test passes.

The problem is wider than one window. Across the whole 542-567 px height band (any width up to 700), the shown bar covers part of the thumbnails on arrival:
- 360x542: 26 px (exactly half);
- 375x543: 25 px;
- 375x548 and 320x548: 20 px;
- 360x560 and 393x560: 8 px.
OLD waits at all of them (/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-super-hot/f4a25b5c-7cd5-585d-b4f3-c7ba36b6c676/scratchpad/gate/c6e/skeptic-gallery-and-bar/out/pa12-band.json).

NEW is far better than C5 (86 px covered), and the ask is on the first screen as ordered. So this is a trade-off, and should-fix, not blocking. The cause is the lane's centre rule for phones, which is looser than the order's 'real overlap (the buttons, no margin)'. The scrolling case is in missed.

Reproduced exactly with pa4.js (/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-super-hot/f4a25b5c-7cd5-585d-b4f3-c7ba36b6c676/scratchpad/gate/c6e/skeptic-gallery-and-bar/out/pa4-a.txt). Plain 768x1024 and 820x1180, /tropos/acid, real wheel and mouse clicks.

